#X obj 653 8 conv.hsl2rgb;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 196 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts HSL color values (Hue \, Saturation
\, Lightness) to RGB values. The hue is given in the range [0 \, 360]
(degrees) \, and saturation and lightness are in the range [0 \, 1].
By default the RGB values are output as integers in the range [0 \,
255] \, with the @float flag they are output as floats in the range
[0 \, 1]. By default the three channel values are sent to three separate
outlets \, if the @pack flag is set \, they are packed into a single
list sent to the first outlet. With the @sync flag \, the object outputs
a new value whenever any inlet changes.;
#X obj 50 322 ui.hsl 0 360 @label HUE @label_inner 1 @show_value 1
